title A floor that refuses a rise is an equality wearing a floor's name
prompt fleet baton -- core infrastructure, Lindy-first crux-first, reds first
rota lap 4198, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; the threshold plus the shape-you-grew, happy-zone and growing-a-language seats. The happy zone's own sentence carried the lap: a refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass. A floor proven only by counts that sit at it has exactly that gap, and this lap found one.
think Opened the card and the ledger. Ten OPEN rows; the card left one question standing in my lane -- plant adoption's remainder=165 counts controls that never plant, so it can never reach zero and nobody can act on it.
think Tried three ways to split the remainder exactly. Every one wanted a rule for telling a plant from a fixture build, and the scan's own header had already measured why each is a proxy that misreads real files. Stopped designing and asked which number is actually the ratchet.
think The answer dissolved the question rather than answering it. sourcing counts the good population and rises with adoption; remainder counts what has not imported the law and includes controls with nothing to import it for. So sourcing is the ratchet and remainder is a report -- no classification needed, which is the rule its author correctly declined to invent.
think Reading the mechanism that holds sourcing is what found it holding the wrong direction. tools/p/plant_witness.rish gated it with assert adoption.out contains "sourcing=13" beneath a paragraph calling it a floor that only ever rises.
obs Proven on metal in a pen before a byte moved. sourcing=14 -- a lane adopting the law -- refuses that assert. And Rishi's contains is a substring reading, so sourcing=130 satisfies sourcing=13; unreachable at 178 controls today, reachable as the corpus grows.
obs The cost is fleet-wide: construction/standing-equipment.kyri seats guard plant at tier lap, so the red lands on every lap of all eight ships until a hand edits the witness. The guard refused the one act it exists to reward.
obs Swept 1,864 tracked witnesses for the same shape. 25 assert a literal non-zero count under prose naming a floor or ratchet; reading all 25, this is the only one whose number is the measurement rather than the declared bound. tally_roster's covered=11 is the near miss and is deliberate -- its own refusal message says a change here is a change to name. A lantern, not a loom.
obs The repair is the tree's own idiom rather than a new one: floor=13 into the scan, compared with -lt, arithmetic read first so a floor never rests on a miscount, verdict=below_floor on a fall, and the witness asserting the word. exec_bit_scan.sh has kept ceiling=57 that way all along.
obs Each floor value in the control's pen is moved by plant_apply, so the control that proves the plant law is itself held by it -- a floor plant that stopped matching would otherwise hand the phase a verdict answering a question it never asked, which is REDS %519 one file in.
obs Both reds of the cold open had one root: a duplicate and a misordered row on the open day shelf, %440 again, from a peer's rebase. index_shelf_repair.sh refuses a duplicate by design, so lifting one row was a hand's and sorting was the tool's. standing_equipment was red only because runs_red counted its peer.
obs Declined, and named on the card: %519's larger half, the 94-and-growing controls that mutate a pen without checking. Adoption is now measurable in the direction it moves, so that sweep is a booked lap rather than a lantern.
loom witness=plant behaviors=36 faults=0 controls=178 sourcing=13 floor=13 remainder=165
loom roster=cold guards_run=174 guards_green=169 guards_red=2 guards_gated=3 seconds=1297
file tools/fixtures/p/plant_adoption_scan.sh the floor and its numeric comparison move here, with the reason the remainder is a report rather than a ratchet
file tools/fixtures/p/plant_control.sh phase 6 -- the floor proven above, at, and below in a real git pen, six behaviors, 30 to 36
file tools/p/plant_witness.rish asserts the scan's verdict word instead of the measurement, so no count is spelled and no substring reading remains
file construction/REDS.md row %582, booked off the fetched spine, cited by stamp until xy binds it
file construction/archive/REDS-a-reading-of-nothing-rows-576.md %576 folded to make room -- the largest BOOKED row on the pin
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front carries the finding and the answered question; elder account shelved
file session-logs/date/20260907/README-index-20260907.md the duplicate row lifted and the shelf sorted -- %440's own repair
recommend keep-going -- the adoption sweep is the next lap in this lane, and it is now measurable in the direction it moves
